.TH LETNGO-RECOMP 1 "2026-10-23" "letsgo-recomp 0.6.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
letsgo\-recomp \- native port of Pok\u00e9mon: Let's Go, Eevee! and Pikachu!
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B letsgo-recomp
.RI [ FOLDER ]
.RB [ \-\-play ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
A native Linux port of the Nintendo Switch games
.BR "Pok\u00e9mon: Let's Go, Eevee!" " and" "Pok\u00e9mon: Let's Go, Pikachu!" ,
made by static recompilation: the games' ARM64 code is translated into C and
compiled for the computer, and a runtime stands in for the Switch (system
services, NVN graphics on Vulkan, audio, controllers). It is not an emulator.
.PP
Without arguments the start screen opens: pick the folder with your own
extracted game files (the one with
.B exefs
and
.BR romfs ),
wait while they are copied and the game code is recompiled for your computer
(once), and press Play.
.PP
With
.I FOLDER
the start screen sets that folder up at once.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-play
Skips the start screen and goes straight to the game (the game files have to be
set up already).
.SH FILES
Everything the program writes lives in
.IR $XDG_DATA_HOME/letsgo-recomp ,
or
.I ~/.local/share/letsgo-recomp
by default:
.TP
.B extracted/
The game's own files (copied from the folder you picked) and the game code
compiled from them.
.TP
.B save/
The game's saves.
.TP
.B cache/
The shader cache, and the textures of the 2x interface.
.TP
.B larecomp.ini
The settings.
.TP
.B lasrecomp.log
The log (the previous run is kept as lasrecomp-prev.log).
.PP
.B LARECOMP_DATA_ROOT
uses another folder for all of it.
.SH REQUIREMENTS
A Vulkan 1.3 driver, and (on x86-64) a CPU with AVX2 (Intel Haswell / 2013 or
newer, AMD Excavator / Zen or newer).
.SH NOTES
No game files are included: you need your own legally obtained copy of the
game, extracted. This is a fan project, not affiliated with Nintendo, The
Pok\u00e9mon Company, Game Freak or Creatures.
.SH SEE ALSO
The project's README and docs/ on the source repository.
